<h1 class="title">Marine tech paths</h1>

<div class="box wide">
  <p>
    The research orders marine commanders went for, ranked by how often the round was won.
    Every group is an opening prefix of up to N <em>distinct</em> researches, in order. Every
    round which starts with that prefix contributes to its record, regardless of any later tech.
    Click a column header to sort.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
    The length selector adds longer prefixes; it never removes shorter ones. For example,
    Armor 1 is counted in every round that begins with Armor 1 at any setting, while Armor 1
    &rarr; Weapons 1 is added when the setting is at least 2. Pick "uncapped" to include every
    opening prefix recorded in the logs.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
    Distress Beacon is ignored (a panic button, not a plan), and the NS1 logs only record when
    a research <em>starts</em>, never when it finishes or which one got cancelled &mdash; so
    this is what commanders went for, not what they got.
  </p>

  <%= form_with url: analysis_tech_paths_path, method: :get, local: true do %>
    <p class="analysis-filters">
      <span>
        <%= label_tag :path_length, 'Techs per path:' %>
        <%= select_tag :path_length,
                       options_for_select(
                         @path_length_options.map { |n| ["up to #{n}", n] } +
                           [['uncapped', MarineTechPathQuery::UNCAPPED_PATH_LENGTH]],
                         @selected_path_length || MarineTechPathQuery::UNCAPPED_PATH_LENGTH
                       ),
                       onchange: 'this.form.requestSubmit()' %>
      </span>
      <span>
        <%= label_tag :min_rounds, 'Minimum rounds per group:' %>
        <%= select_tag :min_rounds,
                       options_for_select(@min_rounds_options.map { |n| [n, n] }, @selected_min_rounds),
                       onchange: 'this.form.requestSubmit()' %>
      </span>
      <span>
        <%= label_tag :result_limit, 'Rows:' %>
        <%= select_tag :result_limit,
                       options_for_select(
                         @result_limit_options.map { |n| ["top #{n}", n] } +
                           [['all qualifying', MarineTechPathQuery::UNCAPPED_RESULT_LIMIT]],
                         @selected_result_limit || MarineTechPathQuery::UNCAPPED_RESULT_LIMIT
                       ),
                       onchange: 'this.form.requestSubmit()' %>
      </span>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if @tech_paths.empty? %>
    <p>
      Among the <%= number_with_delimiter(@paths_found) %> opening paths at this setting, none
      was used in <%= @selected_min_rounds %> or more rounds. Try a lower minimum.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Based on <%= number_with_delimiter(@rounds_analysed) %> rounds. Of the
      <%= number_with_delimiter(@paths_found) %> opening paths at this setting,
      <%= number_with_delimiter(@paths_above_minimum) %> were used in at least
      <%= @selected_min_rounds %> rounds; showing
      <%= @selected_result_limit ? "the best #{@tech_paths.size}" : 'all' %> by win rate below.
    </p>

    <%= sortable_table(
      id: 'marine-tech-paths',
      columns: [
        { key: :path, label: 'Tech path', type: :string,
          sort_value: ->(path) { tech_path_label(path) },
          format: ->(path) { tech_path_display(path) } },
        { key: :rounds, label: 'Rounds', type: :number,
          tooltip: 'How many rounds started with this research order.' },
        { key: :wins, label: 'Wins', type: :number },
        { key: :losses, label: 'Losses', type: :number },
        { key: :win_ratio, label: 'Win %', type: :number,
          format: ->(value) { "#{number_with_precision(value, precision: 1)}%" } }
      ],
      rows: @tech_paths
    ) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
